<title>CHILE: Codelco CEO Villarzu appointed to gov't - radio.</title>
<headline>Codelco CEO Villarzu appointed to gov't - radio.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Juan Villarzu, executive president of Chile's state copper company Codelco, has been appointed as President Eduardo Frei's chief-of-staff, said Radio Cooperativa.</p>
<p>The radio said that the change was part of a cabinet reshuffle by Frei which involved replacing top adviser Genaro Arriagada and three ministers.</p>
<p>The radio's announcement was confirmed shortly afterwards by government spokesman Jose Joaquin Brunner, who added that transport minister Narciso Irueta would also be replaced.</p>
<p>--Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595x212</p>
